Z||000000||Richard Parnell||01-30-2001||05:52 PM||||I've had my V8 going in my 87 SC for a few months now.  I have not been able to find an air filter taht fits under the 67 mustang scoop I put on the trunk.  I even order the smallest one I could find in the Summit catalog, pn EDL-1002 still no fit.  It makes me really uncomfortable running the engine with no filter.  Anyone has a filter that they know will fit?  Thanks<BR>I was going to post pics but when my wife left she took the digital camera so I need to borrow one from a friend.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Archie||01-30-2001||09:40 PM||||What intake manifold are you using? I use the  EDL1002 aircleaner all the time & it will fit under the stock decklid (even without the Mustang scoop).<P>Archie<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Richard Parnell||01-31-2001||04:16 PM||||The manifold is the stock 350 manifold that came with the engine.  The carb is an Edlebrock 600.||||reg||1
