Z||000004||BroCar 87||02-01-2001||12:11 AM||||How is your filter search going??? If that edelbrock air cleaner still doesn't fit (like on BBBad's V8) I found a cleaner that is only 2-1/2" tall. Superflo-II by WEIAND through JEGS part number 925-3003.<BR>Just a suggestion!<P>BroCar 87||||reg||6
Z||000005||stsmithgt||02-01-2001||12:35 PM||||That's exactly the one I was picturing in my head BBBAD. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Though there are some air cleaner housings for low hood clearance, offsetting the air cleaner to one side of the engine, the factory ones I've seen aren't the prettiest things.  Doesn't K&N make something like that?  This address doesn't help the clearance problem, but I thought some of you might look at it to get some ideas. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <A HREF="http://www.autophysics.com/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.autophysics.com/index.html</A> ||||reg||4
Z||000006||Richard Parnell||02-01-2001||01:41 PM||||BBBadGT- The filter you have pictured is the one I got that does not fit.  As a matter of fact when I gave it a test fit and closed the hood (softly I thought) it busted the bolt out of the scoop and now I have to epoxy it back into place.<BR>Love you paint job and attention to detail in the engine compartment.  Mine is not so pretty but still a lot of fun to drive.<BR>BroCar 87-  I'll give the filter you mentioned a try.  <BR>Too bad I'm here in Hawaii and shipping is a hinderance.  I have two different brand new filters now that are of no use to me because they don't fit.  As a matter of fact my old 4 banger is still laying around my mechanics garage and he's grumbling at me to get rid of it.||||reg||7
Z||000007||squid||02-01-2001||10:31 PM||||Try a 1985-1993 FWD Cadillac air cleaner. The diameter is right and the inner supports will rotate in the housing to clear the choke horn. The "wingnut" is a different thread though. You can duct the fresh air tube under the side mounted filter to your fender scoop. Its also practically free.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Archie||02-02-2001||02:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Richard Parnell:<BR><B>BBBadGT- The filter you have pictured is the one I got that does not fit.  As a matter of fact when I gave it a test fit and closed the hood (softly I thought) it busted the bolt out of the scoop and now I have to epoxy it back into place.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you have that aircleaner and don't have a spacer under the carb. etc. then I suspect that the scoop you added actually cut down the area you have to work with.<P>Why don't you take some pictures to share with us?<P>Also, on that type of air cleaner you can trim about 1/2" off the bottom flange to bring it closer to the carb.<P>Over the years I've built like 100 carbed SBC swaps and I've always been able to use that same aircleaner.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000009||V8Fiero||02-02-2001||08:49 AM||||Heres mine with the same filter they are talking about. My carb is factory gm and sticks a little higher than most. So I had to cut out the decklid. I too am running the mustang scoop and it fits underneath perfectly.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/V84_2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/V83_1.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000010||Richard Parnell||02-02-2001||01:53 PM||||Puzzles the heck out of me I have exactly the same scoop setup pictured above.  I'll try trimming the filter like Archie suggests before buying another filter.  Also am thinking of adding some rubber trim all around under the scoop since I don't want to glass it onto the deck.  That may give me the extra 1/4 inch I think I need.||||reg||5
