Z||000013||Richard Parnell||02-12-2001||08:20 PM||||I think I finally figured out why I can't get an air filter to fit under my hood.  I remembered that we had put some sort of adapter plate (about 1/2 inch thick between the Edelbrock 600 carb and the in take manifold.  That takes it just a hair higher than the space the filter needs.  Now what?<BR>I tried modifying the filter I have like Archie suggested but I can't see how to remove any of the sleeve on the filter as he stated.  Maybe I'll try and crush the filter a bit, funky but I really am gettin nervous about running with no filter for so long.||||reg||11
Z||000014||Formula88||02-12-2001||08:40 PM||||You're going to have to ace that adapter plate.  Either get the carb for you intake, or change intake manifolds.  Adapter plates aren't that great for performance, anyway.  I don't recommend them.  But then, who the heck am I?<P>------------------<BR>We all come into this world the same way; naked, screaming, and covered in blood.  If you're lucky, it doesn't have to end there.||||reg||1
